Z||000000||Banzai||09-17-2001||09:13 AM||||Anyone ever replaced the rear main seal while the crank was still in?  What did you use to drive the seal back in? I was thinking maybe a 3.5" PVC Cap. Any suggestions. Thanks<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||09-17-2001||09:37 AM||||They sell a tool..you could use a piece of PVC...or if I don't have anything handy I tap the new one on a bit, then turn the old seal upside down putting it over the new seal and tap it on all the way around.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/simplesig1.gif">  <BR>Did you get your car in my book yet????<BR> <A HREF="http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.animatedconcepts.com/fierobook.htm</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-17-2001||07:07 PM||||Make sure you don't nick the crank getting the ond one out.<P>some correctly sized tubing cut clean on both ends and a block of wood to whack.<P>main thing is it doesn't get bent going in. there's notes on the in the Haynes and Chilton books.||||reg||1
